因为你们当时是制片人。

1034
00:49:04.500 --> 00:49:09.080
And now I remember you were part of like pitching like story ideas and stuff.
我记得你们当时参与了故事构思之类的讨论。

1035
00:49:09.360 --> 00:49:09.800
Yes.
是的。

1036
00:49:09.940 --> 00:49:15.600
And John pitched the idea that Jim would go off to Philly and have this sports job.
约翰提出了让吉姆去费城做体育工作的想法。

1037
00:49:15.600 --> 00:49:22.100
So I didn't check with him, but I have to imagine that maybe, I'm speculating, there
所以我没跟他确认过，但我猜想，我只是推测，可能

1038
00:49:22.100 --> 00:49:25.880
was that little moment in the show Bible and he ran with it.
剧集设定集里有那个小片段，他就顺着这个思路发挥了。

1039
00:49:25.940 --> 00:49:27.200
But that was his pitch.
但这确实是他提出的想法。

1040
00:49:27.300 --> 00:49:31.900
It was not connected in this moment when we shot it, but that's how I think it might have
我们在拍摄这一幕时，它并没有关联，但我认为事情可能就是这样

1041
00:49:31.900 --> 00:49:32.140
happened.
发生的。

1042
00:49:32.240 --> 00:49:32.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1043
00:49:32.480 --> 00:49:35.140
I think the seed had been planted for Philly Jim.
我认为费城吉姆的种子早就种下了。

1044
00:49:35.500 --> 00:49:36.560
Philly Jim.
费城吉姆。

1045
00:49:37.340 --> 00:49:38.900
And here's something crazy.
还有件疯狂的事。

1046
00:49:39.040 --> 00:49:41.000
We'll get to it, but I'll bring it up here.
我们之后会聊到，但我现在先提一下。

1047
00:49:41.000 --> 00:49:45.300
Or when he does move to Philly, there's an electric guitar in his apartment.
当他搬到费城时，他的公寓里确实有一把电吉他。

1048
00:49:45.640 --> 00:49:45.900
Oh!
噢！

1049
00:49:46.220 --> 00:49:50.920
I don't know if he ever learns to play the guitar, but Philly Jim and his guitar, they
我不知道他后来有没有学会弹吉他，但费城吉姆和他的吉他，

1050
00:49:50.920 --> 00:49:51.740
do show up again.
确实再次出现了。

1051
00:49:52.040 --> 00:49:54.540
I mean, it was all connected, you guys.
我的意思是，这一切都是有关联的，伙计们。

1052
00:49:54.540 --> 00:49:55.360
I'm convinced.
我深信不疑。

1053
00:49:55.800 --> 00:50:00.820
Now at 12 minutes, 52 seconds, you guys, Daryl and his team are continuing to rehearse.
现在时间来到12分52秒，伙计们，达里尔和他的团队正在继续排练。

1054
00:50:00.980 --> 00:50:04.700
They've got a new theme song because, you know, Michael gave them notes, right?
他们换了首新主题曲，因为，你知道的，迈克尔给他们提了意见，对吧？

1055
00:50:04.940 --> 00:50:06.800
So now they've written a new song.
所以他们现在写了一首新歌。

1056
00:50:06.980 --> 00:50:09.040
And guess who wrote this version?
猜猜是谁写了这一版？

1057
00:50:09.380 --> 00:50:10.320
Tell us, Ange.
告诉我们吧，安吉。

1058
00:50:10.320 --> 00:50:11.180
Craig Robinson!
克雷格·罗宾逊！

1059
00:50:11.880 --> 00:50:12.340
Yes!
没错！

1060
00:50:12.780 --> 00:50:16.360
And of course, we knew that Craig was an amazing musician.
当然，我们一直都知道克雷格是一位出色的音乐家。

1061
00:50:16.880 --> 00:50:17.480
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1062
00:50:17.740 --> 00:50:18.780
Craig is fantastic.
克雷格太棒了。

1063
00:50:18.960 --> 00:50:20.160
He, like, tours and everything.
他经常去巡演什么的。

1064
00:50:20.320 --> 00:50:21.040
He's great.
他真的很棒。

1065
00:50:21.320 --> 00:50:25.700
In the DVD commentary, they shared that there was a heated debate in the writer's room
在DVD评论音轨里，他们分享说编剧室里曾有过一场激烈的争论，

1066
00:50:25.700 --> 00:50:28.620
about which jingle they should use.
关于该用哪一首广告歌。

1067
00:50:28.700 --> 00:50:31.280
And they ultimately were like, wait, the room was divided.
他们最终觉得，等等，当时意见分成了两派。

1068
00:50:31.420 --> 00:50:32.440
They loved them both.
他们两首都喜欢。

1069
00:50:32.500 --> 00:50:36.240
So they found a way to have them both in the episode, which I thought was great.
所以他们想办法把两首歌都放进了这一集里，我觉得这很棒。

1070
00:50:36.540 --> 00:50:37.380
So fun.
太有趣了。

1071
00:50:37.380 --> 00:50:42.400
Yeah, BJ told me it was cool because it set up this idea that Michael was really obsessive
是啊，BJ告诉我这很酷，因为它确立了迈克尔非常执着这一设定，

1072
00:50:42.400 --> 00:50:44.960
and he kept making them write new versions of the song.
他不停地让他们写新版本的歌。

1073
00:50:45.640 --> 00:50:48.120
There's a line from this scene that I love from Michael.
这一幕里有一句迈克尔的台词我特别喜欢。

1074
00:50:48.280 --> 00:50:49.880
He says, I hate it.
他说，我讨厌它。

1075
00:50:49.960 --> 00:50:51.060
I don't hate it.
我不讨厌它。

1076
00:50:51.140 --> 00:50:52.480
I just don't like it at all.
我只是完全不喜欢它。

1077
00:50:52.480 --> 00:50:53.580
It's terrible.
它太糟糕了。

1078
00:50:56.940 --> 00:51:00.660
One other thing I want to share with you that Craig talks about on the commentary is
还有一件事我想和大家分享，是克雷格在评论音轨里提到的，

1079
00:51:00.660 --> 00:51:04.140
that he only had an hour to rehearse with those guys.
他只有一小时的时间和那些人排练。

1080
00:51:04.400 --> 00:51:06.340
And he said they got it right away.
他说他们立刻就上手了。

1081
00:51:06.560 --> 00:51:07.180
Right away.
立刻就上手了。

1082
00:51:07.280 --> 00:51:08.180
It just fell into place.
一切都水到渠成。

1083
00:51:08.180 --> 00:51:10.140
Except for maybe one moment.
除了可能有一个瞬间。

1084
00:51:10.300 --> 00:51:11.480
We had a fan catch.
我们有一位粉丝发现了。

1085
00:51:11.720 --> 00:51:17.960
Rachel and Jeremy wrote in to say at 13 minutes, 15 seconds, Ed starts to sing at the wrong
瑞秋和杰里米来信说，在13分15秒，埃德开始唱歌的时间不对，

1086
00:51:17.960 --> 00:51:19.780
time and then he almost breaks.
然后他差点笑场了。

1087
00:51:20.000 --> 00:51:20.660
It's the beSt.
这简直太棒了。

1088
00:51:21.340 --> 00:51:23.600
Lady, let's move to the parking lot.
女士们，我们去停车场吧。

1089
00:51:24.140 --> 00:51:27.680
Michael is really losing his patience with people.
迈克尔真的对大家失去了耐心。

1090
00:51:28.000 --> 00:51:28.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1091
00:51:28.260 --> 00:51:30.980
Well, he says, you know, this is a pivotal scene.
嗯，他说，你知道的，这是一个关键场景。

1092
00:51:31.140 --> 00:51:33.580
If they don't get it, the whole thing will fall apart.
如果他们搞砸了，整件事就会分崩离析。

1093
00:51:33.580 --> 00:51:37.560
Yeah, Andy is dressed in some sort of running gear.
没错，安迪穿着某种跑步装备。

1094
00:51:37.880 --> 00:51:42.320
They don't get very far because Phyllis comes back from the mall.
他们没走多远，因为菲利斯从商场回来了。

1095
00:51:42.480 --> 00:51:43.640
She is sobbing.
她在啜泣。

1096
00:51:43.820 --> 00:51:45.400
She is so gutted.
她伤心欲绝。

1097
00:51:45.540 --> 00:51:46.560
She is gutted.
她彻底崩溃了。

1098
00:51:46.760 --> 00:51:51.200
She got kicked out of the mall in front of her friends.
她在朋友面前被赶出了商场。

1099
00:51:51.780 --> 00:51:54.320
All of her friends, I guess, love Sue Grafton.
我猜她所有的朋友都喜欢苏·格拉夫顿。

1100
00:51:54.400 --> 00:51:56.080
They were all there for autographs.
她们当时都在那儿等着签名。

1101
00:51:56.500 --> 00:52:00.700
And Phyllis just wouldn't take no for an answer because Michael told her, don't take no for
菲利斯就是不肯接受拒绝，因为迈克尔告诉她，不要接受

1102
00:52:00.700 --> 00:52:01.160
an answer.
拒绝。

1103
00:52:01.320 --> 00:52:02.620
Get Sue Grafton here.
把苏·格拉夫顿叫来。

1104
00:52:02.620 --> 00:52:05.560
And she kept bugging her and they kicked her out.
她一直缠着对方，结果被赶了出来。

1105
00:52:05.800 --> 00:52:12.920
At the very end of the scene, there is a great little tag where Kevin offers Phyllis a piece
在这一幕的最后，有一个很棒的小彩蛋，凯文递给菲利斯一截

1106
00:52:12.920 --> 00:52:15.380
of tape in lieu of a tissue.
胶带代替纸巾。

1107
00:52:15.840 --> 00:52:17.200
We got some mail about it.
我们收到了一些关于此的邮件。

1108
00:52:17.300 --> 00:52:18.900
Angela from Winston F.
来自温斯顿·F的安吉拉

1109
00:52:19.180 --> 00:52:23.560
and Delina Delano, they wanted to know if this bit was improvised
和德琳娜·德拉诺，她们想知道这个桥段是即兴发挥的

1110
00:52:23.560 --> 00:52:24.460
or scripted.
还是照着剧本演的。

1111
00:52:24.680 --> 00:52:28.840
I texted Brian about it because I don't have the scripts for season four.
我给布莱恩发了短信问这件事，因为我没有第四季的剧本。

1112
00:52:29.080 --> 00:52:31.120
I'm going to guess it was improvised.
我猜是即兴发挥的。

1113
00:52:31.120 --> 00:52:33.800
That seems very much like something Brian would improvise.
这看起来非常像是布莱恩会即兴做出的举动。

1114
00:52:33.980 --> 00:52:35.040
You are correct.
你说对了。

1115
00:52:35.040 --> 00:52:41.340
He told me that originally the scene had ended with the camera just lingering on Phyllis crying,
他告诉我，最初这一幕的结尾是镜头停留在菲利斯哭泣的画面上，

1116
00:52:41.340 --> 00:52:44.960
and he was actually placed a little further in the background with Kate.
而他当时其实和凯特站在更靠后的背景里。

1117
00:52:45.260 --> 00:52:48.000
They were still kind of working on the little running scene.
他们当时还在处理那个小小的奔跑场景。

1118
00:52:48.000 --> 00:52:54.380
But he had the idea at the end to walk up and offer her a piece of tape as a tissue.
但他临时起意，想在最后走过去递给她一截胶带当纸巾。

1119
00:52:54.640 --> 00:52:55.940
Well, they loved it.
嗯，他们很喜欢这个点子。

1120
00:52:56.300 --> 00:53:01.460
So the next time they did the scene, they actually pulled him a little bit more into the foreground
所以下一次拍这一幕时，他们特意把他往前拉了一点，

1121
00:53:01.460 --> 00:53:05.480
and they gave Steve the line, someone give her a tissue.
还给了史蒂夫一句台词：“谁给她拿张纸巾。”

1122
00:53:05.700 --> 00:53:10.080
And then he tore off the piece of tape and that became the button of the scene.
然后他撕下一截胶带，这就成了这一幕的收尾亮点。

1123
00:53:10.520 --> 00:53:11.620
It's so great.
太棒了。

1124
00:53:11.620 --> 00:53:12.540
It's perfect.
太完美了。

1125
00:53:12.900 --> 00:53:17.480
That's such a great example of how our improvisations would work into a scene.
这是一个很好的例子，说明了我们的即兴表演是如何融入场景的。

1126
00:53:17.620 --> 00:53:18.840
We would do them.
我们会先演一遍。

1127
00:53:18.840 --> 00:53:24.860
And then if they liked them, they would say, okay, well, let's draw you into this in a way
如果他们喜欢，就会说，好吧，那我们把你加进去，

1128
00:53:24.860 --> 00:53:28.160
that that creates a fun button or creates a fun moment.
这样能创造出一个有趣的收尾或精彩瞬间。

1129
00:53:28.320 --> 00:53:32.560
I also want to point out, I think I can see Phyllis about to break.
我还想指出一点，我觉得我能看出菲利斯快要笑场了。

1130
00:53:33.120 --> 00:53:35.780
She looks like she is literally about to laugh.
她看起来简直快要笑出来了。

1131
00:53:35.940 --> 00:53:38.580
I don't know how to say this without it sounding weird,
我不知道怎么说才不会听起来很奇怪，

1132
00:53:38.580 --> 00:53:42.720
but I love every time the character of Phyllis is crying.
但我喜欢菲利斯这个角色哭泣的每一个瞬间。

1133
00:53:42.720 --> 00:53:46.800
I, why, why is it so funny?
我，为什么，为什么这这么好笑？

1134
00:53:47.280 --> 00:53:51.020
She's just so good at playing those like emotional beats.
她真的很擅长演绎那些情感起伏的时刻。

1135
00:53:51.020 --> 00:53:52.840
And I just love her.
我真的太爱她了。

1136
00:53:53.000 --> 00:53:54.140
I love it too.
我也很喜欢。

1137
00:53:54.360 --> 00:53:55.360
I really love it.
我真的很喜欢。

1138
00:53:55.860 --> 00:54:00.680
Jenna, Pam is working so hard at her desk, 14 minutes, 49 seconds.
珍娜，帕姆在办公桌前工作得真努力，14分49秒了。

1139
00:54:01.280 --> 00:54:06.680
This Dunder Mifflin logo, she is just really putting her heart and soul into it.
这个邓德·米夫林公司的标志，她真的是全身心地投入其中。

1140
00:54:06.800 --> 00:54:07.940
I admire her.
我很佩服她。

1141
00:54:08.140 --> 00:54:09.860
I think this is the key to success.
我认为这就是成功的关键。

1142
00:54:09.860 --> 00:54:12.220
It doesn't matter how big or small the project,
无论项目大小，

1143
00:54:12.220 --> 00:54:14.140
if you're getting paid or not getting paid.
无论是否有报酬。

1144
00:54:14.360 --> 00:54:17.700
When you're a struggling artist, you have to give every project your all.
当你是一个挣扎中的艺术家时，你必须全力以赴对待每一个项目。

1145
00:54:17.860 --> 00:54:21.580
She has to treat this as if it's going in a Martin Scorsese film.
她必须把这当作是要放进马丁·斯科塞斯的电影里一样对待。

1146
00:54:21.720 --> 00:54:22.740
And she is.
而她确实也是这么做的。

1147
00:54:22.880 --> 00:54:24.140
And I think she's right on.
我觉得她做得对。

1148
00:54:24.640 --> 00:54:24.920
Yes.
没错。

1149
00:54:25.080 --> 00:54:27.080
And so much so that she doesn't go home.
甚至投入到连家都不回了。

1150
00:54:27.480 --> 00:54:28.740
Jim's like, are you coming?
吉姆问她：“你要走了吗？”

1151
00:54:29.040 --> 00:54:31.080
And she's like, no, I'm going to stay.
然后她说，不，我要留下来。

1152
00:54:31.320 --> 00:54:32.300
I have a question.
我有个问题。

1153
00:54:32.560 --> 00:54:34.800
Is this a little hint that they're living together?
这算不算暗示他们住在一起了？

1154
00:54:35.440 --> 00:54:35.880
Interesting.
有意思。

1155
00:54:36.220 --> 00:54:37.940
I never thought they were living together,
我从没觉得他们住在一起，

1156
00:54:37.940 --> 00:54:40.340
but I think they're in that phase of their relationship
但我认为他们正处于恋爱中的那个阶段，

1157
00:54:40.340 --> 00:54:43.240
where they're staying over at each other's places a lot.
就是经常在对方家里过夜。

1158
00:54:43.400 --> 00:54:47.200
Like, they might as well be living together, but I don't think they are yet.
就像是，他们跟住在一起也差不多了，但我觉得还没到那一步。

1159
00:54:47.560 --> 00:54:50.640
Well, poor Jim has to ride home now with Meredith.
好吧，可怜的吉姆现在得搭梅雷迪思的车回家了。

1160
00:54:51.060 --> 00:54:51.600
He does.
确实。

1161
00:54:51.720 --> 00:54:58.360
And then Pam, we reveal, has slept in the office overnight.
然后我们发现，帕姆在办公室过了一夜。

1162
00:54:58.360 --> 00:55:05.820
And then the next morning opens with Pam waking up to a phone call from Jim.
第二天早上，帕姆被吉姆的电话吵醒。

1163
00:55:06.340 --> 00:55:07.500
He got her breakfaSt.
他给她买了早餐。

1164
00:55:07.800 --> 00:55:08.440
He got her breakfaSt.
他给她买了早餐。

1165
00:55:08.620 --> 00:55:12.080
And in the commentary, they said there was a big debate in the writer's room about,
在评论音轨里，他们说编剧室里曾有过一场大争论，

1166
00:55:12.380 --> 00:55:14.480
does he bring her orange juice or coffee?
他到底是该带橙汁还是咖啡？

1167
00:55:14.720 --> 00:55:17.100
I don't remember seeing either on the desk.
我不记得桌上有这两样东西中的任何一个。

1168
00:55:17.280 --> 00:55:22.060
There's a cup of orange juice and what looks like some kind of breakfast, maybe sandwich.
桌上有杯橙汁，还有看起来像是某种早餐的东西，可能是三明治。

1169
00:55:22.540 --> 00:55:22.820
Yeah.
没错。

1170
00:55:23.020 --> 00:55:27.680
I'm guessing it's from McDonald's because Jim says that Creed ate the hash browns.
我猜是麦当劳的，因为吉姆说克里德吃了薯饼。

1171
00:55:27.680 --> 00:55:28.060
Yes.
是的。

1172
00:55:28.280 --> 00:55:33.660
But they felt like orange juice was just a sweeter token than coffee.
但他们觉得比起咖啡，橙汁作为心意更贴心。

1173
00:55:33.900 --> 00:55:34.820
That's what they decided.
他们就是这么决定的。

1174
00:55:35.020 --> 00:55:37.460
But no detail went unturned, you guys.
但伙计们，每一个细节都没被放过。

1175
00:55:37.620 --> 00:55:40.280
This is the point, that there was a whole conversation about,
重点在于，他们专门讨论过，

1176
00:55:40.440 --> 00:55:42.480
should there be orange juice or coffee?
到底是该选橙汁还是咖啡？

1177
00:55:42.640 --> 00:55:45.120
That's how much thought was put into all of these moments.
这些时刻背后倾注了多少心血啊。

1178
00:55:45.540 --> 00:55:48.520
Well, you know, Pam does not regularly drink coffee, you know?
嗯，你知道，帕姆平时不怎么喝咖啡，对吧？

1179
00:55:48.580 --> 00:55:49.440
She drinks tea.
她喝茶。

1180
00:55:49.440 --> 00:55:51.640
So I think orange juice was the right choice.
所以我认为选橙汁是对的。

1181
00:55:51.820 --> 00:55:52.000
Yeah.
没错。

1182
00:55:52.360 --> 00:55:57.200
Well, Pam explains in a talking head that she worked until 2.45 a.m.
帕姆在采访中解释说她工作到了凌晨两点四十五分。

1183
00:55:57.200 --> 00:56:01.820
And then she had to decide between spending the night with Michael and Dwight in the office
然后她必须在和迈克尔、德怀特一起在办公室过夜，

1184
00:56:01.820 --> 00:56:06.660
or risk driving home and falling asleep at the wheel and dying in a fiery car wreck.
还是冒着开车回家时睡着并死于车祸的风险之间做选择。

1185
00:56:06.800 --> 00:56:09.180
She passed out on her keyboard trying to decide.
她在做决定时直接趴在键盘上睡着了。

1186
00:56:09.420 --> 00:56:12.780
So this was the talking head with Jason that I could not get through.
所以这就是我和杰森拍的那段采访，我一直笑场拍不下去。

1187
00:56:13.000 --> 00:56:15.200
I could not get through that last line.
我一直没法顺利说完最后那句台词。

1188
00:56:15.200 --> 00:56:17.840
I passed out on my keyboard trying to decide.
我在做决定时直接趴在键盘上睡着了。

1189
00:56:18.120 --> 00:56:19.960
Because there's this little pause.
因为中间有那么一小段停顿。

1190
00:56:20.200 --> 00:56:24.360
And in that pause, the anticipation of that last line would make us laugh.
而在那段停顿里，对最后那句台词的期待总是让我们笑场。

1191
00:56:24.360 --> 00:56:26.420
This is something you guys should all know.
这件事你们都应该知道。

1192
00:56:26.660 --> 00:56:29.560
I have found over the years, and I think, Jenna, you'll agree with me,
这些年来我发现，而且我想，珍娜，你也会同意我的看法，

1193
00:56:29.740 --> 00:56:34.520
it's the pauses in comedy that get you almost more than the line.
喜剧里的停顿往往比台词本身更能戳中笑点。

1194
00:56:34.680 --> 00:56:38.800
When Steve would pause before saying something ridiculous as Michael,
当史蒂夫在以迈克尔的身份说出荒唐话之前停顿一下时，

1195
00:56:39.060 --> 00:56:42.620
it was that three-second pause that would have us all on the floor.
那三秒钟的停顿总能让我们笑得前仰后合。

1196
00:56:42.760 --> 00:56:47.240
It was like this collective moment where we all knew what was coming and we couldn't bear it.
那就像是一个集体的瞬间，我们都知道接下来会发生什么，却又无法忍受那种期待感。

1197
00:56:47.380 --> 00:56:48.580
A hundred percent.
百分之百同意。

1198
00:56:48.960 --> 00:56:50.200
I have a catch.
我发现了一个穿帮点。

1199
00:56:50.420 --> 00:56:50.860
Okay.
好的。

1200
00:56:50.860 --> 00:56:55.240
In an upcoming episode, it is going to be revealed that Pam wears glasses.
在接下来的一集里，大家会发现帕姆戴眼镜了。

1201
00:56:55.580 --> 00:56:58.600
Remember, because she's going to have to wear her spare pair to work.
记住，因为她得戴着备用眼镜去上班。

1202
00:56:58.740 --> 00:56:59.040
Right.
对。

1203
00:56:59.300 --> 00:57:02.000
Does that mean that Pam just slept in her contacts?
那是不是意味着帕姆刚才戴着隐形眼镜睡觉了？

1204
00:57:02.480 --> 00:57:03.240
Can you do that?
那样可以吗？

1205
00:57:03.240 --> 00:57:05.800
I don't wear contacts, but I think you're not supposed to do that.
我不戴隐形眼镜，但我记得好像不应该那样做。

1206
00:57:05.880 --> 00:57:07.140
I think that's a big no-no.
我觉得那是绝对禁止的。

1207
00:57:07.160 --> 00:57:08.980
I think it dries your eyeballs out or something.
我想那会把眼球弄干什么的。

1208
00:57:09.380 --> 00:57:13.460
I mean, also, like, does Pam keep a toothbrush and toothpaste in her desk?
我是说，还有，帕姆会在办公桌里放牙刷和牙膏吗？

1209
00:57:13.640 --> 00:57:14.900
I thought the same thing.
我也这么想。

1210
00:57:14.900 --> 00:57:20.720
And finally, before we move on from this little moment, what has Dwight done to the couch?
最后，在我们离开这个小插曲之前，德怀特对沙发做了什么？

1211
00:57:21.140 --> 00:57:28.520
He turned it on its side, and then he has taken all the cushions off, and he is sleeping under the cushions.
他把它侧翻过来，然后把所有坐垫都拆了，他正睡在坐垫下面。

1212
00:57:28.600 --> 00:57:30.260
It's so odd.
太奇怪了。

1213
00:57:30.400 --> 00:57:33.420
I think he got cold, and he was trying to make a cushion blanket.
我觉得他冷了，想用坐垫做个毯子。

1214
00:57:33.660 --> 00:57:34.800
I guess.
我想是吧。

1215
00:57:35.100 --> 00:57:36.520
It's very strange.
这真的很奇怪。

1216
00:57:37.800 --> 00:57:39.540
I feel like he's done it before.
我觉得他以前肯定干过这种事。

1217
00:57:39.560 --> 00:57:41.740
He has a system for that couch.
他对那张沙发有一套自己的系统。

1218
00:57:41.740 --> 00:57:52.120
What we know now, Angela, is probably that Dwight, Pam, and Michael all have really bad breath, because I can't imagine any of them had toothbrushes.
安吉拉，我们现在知道的是，德怀特、帕姆和迈克尔肯定都有严重的口臭，因为我无法想象他们谁带了牙刷。

1219
00:57:52.300 --> 00:57:52.560
No.
没错。

1220
00:57:52.860 --> 00:57:53.980
Maybe Michael, though.
不过迈克尔也许带了。

1221
00:57:54.180 --> 00:57:59.120
I feel like maybe Michael keeps one in his cabinet, so he's got fresh breath, but I mean.
我觉得迈克尔可能在柜子里放了一把，所以他口气清新，但我是说。

1222
00:57:59.260 --> 00:58:04.660
My guess is Michael has a whole change of clothes in that cabinet, and he's got some boxer shorts, a pair of socks.
我猜迈克尔在那个柜子里放了一整套换洗衣物，还有平角内裤和一双袜子。

1223
00:58:05.020 --> 00:58:05.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1224
00:58:05.340 --> 00:58:05.980
He's prepared.
他准备得很充分。

1225
00:58:06.460 --> 00:58:08.300
Should we move into the break room?
我们要去休息室了吗？

1226
00:58:08.440 --> 00:58:10.640
Because Andy has some news for Dwight.
因为安迪有消息要告诉德怀特。

1227
00:58:10.640 --> 00:58:13.980
Oh, Operation Fallen Angel turned a corner.
哦，“堕落天使行动”有了转机。

1228
00:58:14.160 --> 00:58:20.220
I guess while they were doing their form of necking, he's kissing her earlobe, and she says,
我猜在他们那种亲热的时候，他在亲吻她的耳垂，然后她说，

1229
00:58:20.500 --> 00:58:21.660
O.D.
O.D.（安迪）。

1230
00:58:22.360 --> 00:58:25.140
Dwight's face lights up.
德怀特的脸亮了起来。

1231
00:58:25.420 --> 00:58:26.220
Lights up.
亮了起来。

1232
00:58:26.380 --> 00:58:32.100
Andy thinks that this is because of his name, Andy, but we all know the truth.
安迪以为这是因为他的名字安迪，但我们都知道真相。

1233
00:58:32.360 --> 00:58:33.780
Andy, what a stretch.
安迪，这联想也太牵强了。

1234
00:58:33.780 --> 00:58:37.060
Why would you single out one letter of your name?
你为什么偏偏挑出名字里的一个字母？

1235
00:58:37.300 --> 00:58:38.280
O-A.
O-A。

1236
00:58:38.480 --> 00:58:39.260
O-N.
O-N。

1237
00:58:39.540 --> 00:58:40.240
O-D.
O-D。

1238
00:58:40.580 --> 00:58:41.400
O-Y.
O-Y。

1239
00:58:42.100 --> 00:58:42.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1240
00:58:42.640 --> 00:58:52.220
But Dwight then has this very fun moment where he is rejoicing with Andy over Angela calling out O-D.
但德怀特随后有一个非常有趣的时刻，他因为安吉拉喊出“O.D.”而与安迪一起欢呼雀跃。

1241
00:58:52.580 --> 00:58:53.780
There's hope, Dwight.
有希望了，德怀特。

1242
00:58:54.180 --> 00:58:55.620
I love the next scene.
我喜欢接下来的那一幕。

1243
00:58:55.800 --> 00:58:58.260
Michael sends the commercial to corporate.
迈克尔把广告发给了公司总部。

1244
00:58:58.540 --> 00:59:00.140
He's like, they'll probably watch it right away.
他说，他们可能会马上看。

1245
00:59:00.140 --> 00:59:01.020
I know I would.
我知道我会的。

1246
00:59:01.020 --> 00:59:01.520
Yeah.
是啊。

1247
00:59:01.840 --> 00:59:02.960
And he's like, I'm not going to call him.
他说，我不会给他打电话。

1248
00:59:03.080 --> 00:59:03.660
I'm not going to bug him.
我不会去烦他。

1249
00:59:03.820 --> 00:59:05.880
And then he calls him 10 seconds later.
结果十秒钟后他就打过去了。

1250
00:59:06.120 --> 00:59:06.680
I know.
我知道。

1251
00:59:06.800 --> 00:59:07.280
It's perfect.
这太完美了。

1252
00:59:07.520 --> 00:59:08.360
We've all been there.
我们都有过这种经历。

1253
00:59:08.540 --> 00:59:08.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1254
00:59:08.900 --> 00:59:13.220
We've all sent somebody something we've written, something you've worked on.
我们都曾给别人发过自己写的东西，发过自己用心创作的东西。

1255
00:59:13.980 --> 00:59:16.240
And then you just wait and wait.
然后你就只能在那儿干等，一直等。

1256
00:59:16.240 --> 00:59:20.200
And then you do that thing in your head where you're like, oh my gosh, what if my email was down?
接着你就会开始胡思乱想，比如，天哪，万一我的邮件没发出去怎么办？

1257
00:59:20.360 --> 00:59:20.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1258
00:59:20.580 --> 00:59:21.600
What if they never got it?
万一他们根本没收到呢？

1259
00:59:22.140 --> 00:59:23.300
Oh, I should call them.
噢，我应该给他们打个电话。

1260
00:59:23.460 --> 00:59:25.240
I should text them and just nudge them.
我应该发条短信提醒他们一下。

1261
00:59:25.420 --> 00:59:25.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1262
00:59:26.100 --> 00:59:27.200
10 days later.
十天后。

1263
00:59:27.420 --> 00:59:28.340
And this was a big deal.
这可是件大事。

1264
00:59:28.480 --> 00:59:30.740
This kind of time jump we hadn't done in the show before.
这种时间跨度是我们剧集里以前没用过的。

1265
00:59:30.980 --> 00:59:32.020
It's very strange.
这非常奇怪。

1266
00:59:32.200 --> 00:59:37.760
They had that little bit of an unwritten rule that the ideal episode happened over one day.
我们之前有个不成文的规定，就是理想的单集剧情应该发生在一整天之内。

1267
00:59:37.960 --> 00:59:38.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1268
00:59:38.280 --> 00:59:39.560
We didn't always keep to it.
我们并不总是遵守这个规定。

1269
00:59:39.680 --> 00:59:42.140
But for the most part, our episodes happened in one day.
但大部分情况下，我们的剧情都是在一天内发生的。

1270
00:59:42.300 --> 00:59:43.880
So this says 10 days later.
所以这里写着“十天后”。

1271
00:59:44.020 --> 00:59:44.980
It didn't bump me, Jenna.
我没觉得有什么突兀的，珍娜。

1272
00:59:45.300 --> 00:59:45.540
No.
没有。

1273
00:59:45.740 --> 00:59:46.800
I was fine with it.
我完全能接受。

1274
00:59:46.800 --> 00:59:52.900
And Michael is saying, well, welcome to the world premiere of the Corporate Crap FeSt.
迈克尔当时说，欢迎来到“企业烂片节”全球首映礼。

1275
00:59:53.380 --> 00:59:53.960
Yeah.
是啊。

1276
00:59:54.140 --> 00:59:55.760
They did not pick his commercial.
他们没选中他的广告。

1277
00:59:56.060 --> 00:59:56.860
They did not.
确实没选中。

1278
00:59:57.060 --> 01:00:01.340
The whole gang has gathered at Poor Richard's Pub to watch the Corporate Crap FeSt.
大伙儿都聚在“可怜理查德酒吧”观看“企业烂片节”。

1279
01:00:01.700 --> 01:00:02.100
Yeah.
是啊。

1280
01:00:02.280 --> 01:00:02.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1281
01:00:02.780 --> 01:00:03.940
They watch it.
他们看了。

1282
01:00:04.120 --> 01:00:04.940
They're delighted.
他们很高兴。

1283
01:00:05.280 --> 01:00:07.660
They are in the last five seconds.
就在最后五秒钟。

1284
01:00:07.660 --> 01:00:10.220
It's the same commercial as the Nashua branch.
那广告和纳舒厄分部的一模一样。

1285
01:00:10.380 --> 01:00:14.880
But this time it ends with everyone at Dunder Mifflin Scranton waving.
但这次结尾是邓德·米夫林斯克兰顿分部的所有人都在挥手。

1286
01:00:15.420 --> 01:00:16.440
On the roof.
在屋顶上。

1287
01:00:17.100 --> 01:00:17.900
On the roof.
在屋顶上。

1288
01:00:18.020 --> 01:00:23.320
I guess that was Michael's big creative contribution is we'll wave from the roof.
我想这就是迈克尔最大的创意贡献了，就是让我们在屋顶上挥手。

1289
01:00:23.500 --> 01:00:23.660
Yeah.
是啊。

1290
01:00:23.820 --> 01:00:24.960
We won't be in the parking lot.
我们不会在停车场里。

1291
01:00:25.100 --> 01:00:26.260
We're going to go on the rooftop.
我们要去屋顶上。

1292
01:00:27.260 --> 01:00:28.960
Jenna, do you remember I wasn't there that day?
珍娜，你还记得那天我不在场吗？

1293
01:00:29.700 --> 01:00:30.140
No.
不记得。

1294
01:00:30.440 --> 01:00:31.160
I know.
我知道。

1295
01:00:31.460 --> 01:00:33.560
Mindy and I both were not there that day.
敏迪和我都不是那天在场的。

1296
01:00:34.180 --> 01:00:36.560
We had to be superimposed in.
我们是后期合成进去的。

1297
01:00:36.740 --> 01:00:38.420
We never went up on the roof.
我们根本没上过屋顶。

1298
01:00:38.880 --> 01:00:40.360
We just did a wave.
我们只是对着镜头挥了挥手。

1299
01:00:40.460 --> 01:00:42.800
They sort of cheated it in the parking lot.
他们在停车场里凑合拍了一下。

1300
01:00:42.800 --> 01:00:47.020
And then they did a little fancy editing and put us in the shot.
然后通过一点精巧的剪辑把我们放进了画面里。

1301
01:00:47.280 --> 01:00:53.240
That is crazy because I did look specifically to see if everyone was in there and you're
这太疯狂了，因为我特意看了看大家是否都在那儿，而你

1302
01:00:53.240 --> 01:00:53.520
there.
在那儿。

1303
01:00:53.660 --> 01:00:58.520
But if you look closely and I screen grabbed it, Mindy and I are kind of awkwardly off
但如果你仔细看，我截了图，敏迪和我有点尴尬地站在

1304
01:00:58.520 --> 01:00:59.320
to the side.
一边。

1305
01:00:59.560 --> 01:01:00.400
Do you see the gap?
你看到那个空隙了吗？

1306
01:01:00.680 --> 01:01:01.960
That is crazy.
太疯狂了。

1307
01:01:02.480 --> 01:01:05.640
That's like that crazy thing they do when someone has to play their own twin.
就像他们让某人扮演自己的双胞胎时做的那种疯狂事一样。

1308
01:01:06.380 --> 01:01:06.860
Exactly.
没错。

1309
01:01:06.860 --> 01:01:09.520
Well, you can see it at 18 minutes, 10 seconds.
嗯，你可以在18分10秒的时候看到。

1310
01:01:10.020 --> 01:01:12.400
And I know why I couldn't be there that day.
我知道那天我为什么不能去。

1311
01:01:12.520 --> 01:01:14.100
I can't remember why Mindy couldn't be there.
我不记得敏迪为什么不能去。

1312
01:01:14.200 --> 01:01:21.440
But I had one of my first OBGYN appointments because I was pregnant.
但我当时有第一次妇产科预约，因为我怀孕了。

1313
01:01:22.480 --> 01:01:29.020
Lady, I was wondering if you were going to share that in this episode because I just want
天哪，我一直在想你这集会不会分享这件事，因为我只想

1314
01:01:29.020 --> 01:01:35.560
you to know I can see, I'm getting goosebumps, I can see your glow.
让你知道我看得出来，我起鸡皮疙瘩了，我能看到你散发的光芒。

1315
01:01:35.860 --> 01:01:36.260
Really?
真的吗？

1316
01:01:36.640 --> 01:01:38.020
In this whole episode.
整整一集都是。

1317
01:01:38.220 --> 01:01:38.580
Yes.
是的。

1318
01:01:38.820 --> 01:01:42.000
I clocked it the minute I put this episode on.
我一打开这集就注意到了。

1319
01:01:42.140 --> 01:01:47.740
I was like, oh my gosh, this is the episode where Angela was pregnant.
我当时想，天哪，这就是安吉拉怀孕的那一集。

1320
01:01:48.120 --> 01:01:48.520
Yes.
是的。

1321
01:01:48.840 --> 01:01:50.100
And I had this appointment.
我当时有这个预约。

1322
01:01:50.240 --> 01:01:51.680
I guess I couldn't move it.
我想我没法改期。

1323
01:01:51.920 --> 01:01:53.560
And, you know, Kent was really sweet.
而且，你知道，肯特人真的很好。

1324
01:01:53.660 --> 01:01:54.720
He was like, oh, it's fine, Angela.
他说，噢，没关系，安吉拉。

1325
01:01:54.860 --> 01:01:55.640
Well, don't worry about it.
别担心。

1326
01:01:55.680 --> 01:01:56.400
Go to your appointment.
去忙你的预约吧。

1327
01:01:56.700 --> 01:01:56.960
Yeah.
是啊。

1328
01:01:57.080 --> 01:01:58.300
That's why I wasn't in it.
这就是我没在那场戏里的原因。

1329
01:01:58.300 --> 01:02:03.680
Well, I'll never forget, Angela, because you told me you were pregnant in my trailer at
嗯，我永远不会忘记，安吉拉，因为你是在我的拖车里告诉我你怀孕的，

1330
01:02:03.680 --> 01:02:04.140
work.
在工作的时候。

1331
01:02:04.280 --> 01:02:04.600
Yes.
是的。

1332
01:02:04.740 --> 01:02:06.760
This is one of my favorite moments of our whole friendship.
这是我们整个友谊中最喜欢的时刻之一。

1333
01:02:06.920 --> 01:02:09.660
We were in Jenna's trailer having lunch, as we often did.
我们当时在珍娜的拖车里吃午饭，就像我们经常做的那样。

1334
01:02:09.780 --> 01:02:11.940
And you were telling me a whole story.
你当时在给我讲一个完整的故事。

1335
01:02:11.940 --> 01:02:13.540
I think it was about your cat.
我想是关于你的猫的。

1336
01:02:13.860 --> 01:02:14.860
Was it about your cat?
是关于你的猫吗？

1337
01:02:15.180 --> 01:02:17.620
Lady, I remember I was done with lunch.
天哪，我记得我吃完午饭了。

1338
01:02:17.740 --> 01:02:18.500
You were still eating.
你还在吃。

1339
01:02:18.520 --> 01:02:23.880
And I was doing these little five-pound weights, little bicep curls.
我当时在做这些五磅重的小哑铃，做二头肌弯举。

1340
01:02:24.160 --> 01:02:24.420
Yes.
是的。

1341
01:02:24.420 --> 01:02:26.720
You were telling me a whole story while lifting weights.
你一边举重一边给我讲故事。

1342
01:02:26.720 --> 01:02:28.020
You were very passionate.
你当时非常投入。

1343
01:02:28.300 --> 01:02:32.620
I'll never forget it because I go on and on and on and on.
我永远不会忘记，因为我一直在说个不停。

1344
01:02:32.740 --> 01:02:34.520
I'm pumping my arMs.
我挥舞着双臂。

1345
01:02:34.520 --> 01:02:39.180
And then I get finished and you say, well, I have some news.
然后我讲完了，你说，嗯，我有个消息。

1346
01:02:39.640 --> 01:02:40.640
I'm pregnant.
我怀孕了。

1347
01:02:40.820 --> 01:02:44.500
And I just dropped the weights and I screamed.
我直接扔掉了哑铃，尖叫了起来。

1348
01:02:44.880 --> 01:02:49.740
And our AD came over to the trailer because I think they thought someone had had an accident.
我们的助理导演跑到了拖车旁，因为我想他们以为有人出事了。

1349
01:02:49.960 --> 01:02:52.680
There was this huge thud followed by a scream.
先是一声巨响，接着是一声尖叫。

1350
01:02:52.680 --> 01:02:57.040
And then you said to me, Ange, why didn't you interrupt me?
然后你对我说，安吉，你为什么不打断我？

1351
01:02:57.160 --> 01:02:59.360
I'm just rambling on about nothing.
我刚才只是在胡言乱语，没说什么正经事。

1352
01:02:59.360 --> 01:03:01.960
And you're sitting on this big piece of information.
而你却一直守着这么重要的消息。

1353
01:03:02.160 --> 01:03:04.000
Why did you let me go on and on?
你为什么让我一直说个不停呢？

1354
01:03:04.100 --> 01:03:06.600
And I said, well, I wanted to hear your story.
我说，好吧，我是想听听你的故事。

1355
01:03:06.860 --> 01:03:07.520
My God.
天哪。

1356
01:03:07.860 --> 01:03:08.880
So funny.
太搞笑了。

1357
01:03:09.060 --> 01:03:10.460
I was just so happy for you.
我当时真的为你感到高兴。

1358
01:03:10.460 --> 01:03:12.220
I knew how much you wanted to be a mother.
我知道你有多想成为一名母亲。

1359
01:03:12.380 --> 01:03:17.980
And I could just, I'm tearing up right now thinking about it because you are such a good
我简直……我现在想到这些都要热泪盈眶了，因为你真的是一个很好的

1360
01:03:17.980 --> 01:03:18.280
mother.
母亲。

1361
01:03:18.500 --> 01:03:20.440
You are a born nurturer.
你天生就是个会照顾人的人。

1362
01:03:21.420 --> 01:03:23.480
And I was just so happy for you.
我当时真的为你感到高兴。

1363
01:03:24.120 --> 01:03:25.760
I knew how much you wanted that.
我知道你有多渴望那个。

1364
01:03:27.320 --> 01:03:31.980
But yes, when I watched this episode, I knew right away, oh, this is the one.
但是没错，当我看到这一集时，我立刻就意识到，噢，就是这一集了。

1365
01:03:32.040 --> 01:03:33.780
And I didn't know if you were going to share it or not.
我不知道你会不会分享它。

1366
01:03:33.820 --> 01:03:34.340
So I waited.
所以我一直在等。

1367
01:03:34.900 --> 01:03:36.720
Yes, I was never up on the roof.
是的，我从来没上过那个屋顶。

1368
01:03:36.920 --> 01:03:39.480
Never, never in the whole series.
从来没有，整部剧里一次都没有。

1369
01:03:39.960 --> 01:03:40.400
Wow.
哇。

1370
01:03:40.600 --> 01:03:41.000
I know.
我知道。

1371
01:03:41.140 --> 01:03:42.920
Your old hat at being up on the roof.
你可是上屋顶的老手了。

1372
01:03:43.080 --> 01:03:43.580
Oh, man.
天呐。

1373
01:03:44.040 --> 01:03:45.720
So Jim does a very sweet thing.
吉姆做了一件非常贴心的事。

1374
01:03:46.020 --> 01:03:51.420
He asked the bartender if he will play their commercial, the one that they all made together.
他问酒保愿不愿意播放他们的广告，就是他们一起拍的那支。

1375
01:03:51.580 --> 01:03:52.660
He hands him the disc.
他把光盘递给了他。

1376
01:03:52.780 --> 01:03:55.260
And Michael is so moved by this.
迈克尔被这一幕深深打动了。

1377
01:03:55.760 --> 01:03:56.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1378
01:03:56.260 --> 01:04:00.540
Well, you know, the bartender slash waiter guy was played by Drew Powell.
嗯，你知道，那个酒保兼服务员是由德鲁·鲍威尔饰演的。

1379
01:04:01.020 --> 01:04:03.820
You guys might recognize him from Gotham.
你们可能在《哥谭》里见过他。

1380
01:04:03.960 --> 01:04:05.520
He's a regular on Gotham.
他是《哥谭》的常驻演员。

1381
01:04:05.660 --> 01:04:09.520
He also played Eddie Murdoch from the Monk episode, Mr. Monk Can't See a Thing.
他还演过《神探阿蒙》那一集《阿蒙先生看不见东西》里的埃迪·默多克。

1382
01:04:09.820 --> 01:04:12.440
And here's my crossover connection with Drew.
这就是我和德鲁之间的交集。

1383
01:04:12.880 --> 01:04:18.020
Drew and I played husband and wife in a Lifetime movie called Terror in the Woods.
我和德鲁在一部名为《林中惊魂》的Lifetime电影里演过夫妻。

1384
01:04:18.440 --> 01:04:19.660
Oh, I remember this.
噢，我记得这个。

1385
01:04:19.980 --> 01:04:22.200
Yes, we filmed it in Atlanta.
是的，我们在亚特兰大拍的。

1386
01:04:22.240 --> 01:04:24.440
And so we hung out and spent some time together.
所以我们当时经常待在一起。

1387
01:04:24.440 --> 01:04:29.980
And when I got back to L.A., we realized our kids were at the same elementary school.
等我回到洛杉矶后，我们发现我们的孩子在同一所小学上学。

1388
01:04:30.220 --> 01:04:31.220
You're kidding me.
你在开玩笑吧。

1389
01:04:31.300 --> 01:04:33.740
No, our sons went to elementary school together.
没有，我们的儿子上的是同一所小学。

1390
01:04:33.740 --> 01:04:37.260
And then I started seeing him at morning assembly meetings and all kinds of stuff.
后来我在晨会和其他各种活动上经常见到他。

1391
01:04:37.400 --> 01:04:38.360
That's so crazy.
太疯狂了。

1392
01:04:38.640 --> 01:04:39.240
I know.
我知道。

1393
01:04:39.520 --> 01:04:40.420
What a small world.
世界真小。

1394
01:04:40.420 --> 01:04:46.040
So everybody watches Michael's version of the commercial, and it's so charming.
大家都看了迈克尔版本的广告，非常迷人。

1395
01:04:46.520 --> 01:04:48.840
Everyone reacts really well to it.
大家的反应都很好。

1396
01:04:48.980 --> 01:04:58.020
And there was a decision to be made as to whether or not when we watch Michael's commercial, we were going to be kind of embarrassed and like, oh, Michael.
当时我们面临一个抉择，就是当我们看迈克尔的广告时，我们是该表现得有点尴尬，觉得“噢，迈克尔”这样，

1397
01:04:58.020 --> 01:05:00.160
Or if we were all going to love it.
还是我们大家都该喜欢它。

1398
01:05:00.540 --> 01:05:01.980
And Jason talked about this.
杰森谈到过这一点。

1399
01:05:02.160 --> 01:05:05.720
It was really important to him that they pick the sweeter ending.
对他来说，选择更温馨的结局非常重要。

1400
01:05:05.960 --> 01:05:07.140
Here's what he had to say.
听听他是怎么说的。

1401
01:05:07.660 --> 01:05:10.160
There was an opportunity for a tender ending.
当时有一个机会可以做一个温情的结局。

1402
01:05:10.840 --> 01:05:17.980
And I got the sense that the writing staff of The Office was hesitant to do too many of those.
我感觉到《办公室》的编剧团队对于做太多这种结局有些犹豫。

1403
01:05:18.140 --> 01:05:21.580
That there's this kind of traditional television episode where it's funny throughout.
因为这是一种传统的电视集，通常从头到尾都要搞笑。

1404
01:05:21.800 --> 01:05:23.180
It has opportunity for satire.
它有讽刺的机会。

1405
01:05:23.460 --> 01:05:27.260
And then towards the end, you have some sort of tender denouement.
然后在结尾处，你会有一种温情的收场。

1406
01:05:27.520 --> 01:05:29.420
And that they didn't want to be doing this every time.
他们不想每次都这样做。

1407
01:05:29.500 --> 01:05:31.380
But I really wanted that for this spot.
但我真的很想在这一集里实现这一点。

1408
01:05:31.380 --> 01:05:37.200
I really wanted the episode to end in a bar where the cast is watching the commercial together.
我真的很想让这一集在酒吧里结束，演员们聚在一起看广告。

1409
01:05:37.580 --> 01:05:39.140
And they bond over it.
他们因此而建立了感情。

1410
01:05:39.240 --> 01:05:42.580
And there's something really lovely about people who come together to make something.
人们聚在一起创作某样东西，这真的很美好。

1411
01:05:42.760 --> 01:05:45.120
That was really important to me because that's an idea I know really well.
这对我来说非常重要，因为这个概念我非常熟悉。

1412
01:05:45.220 --> 01:05:55.060
I think anyone who's ever done a high school play or made a high school video or done anything creative knows what it feels like when outsiders come together to make something.
我想任何演过高中话剧、拍过高中视频或做过任何创意工作的人，都知道当一群局外人聚在一起创作时是什么感觉。

1413
01:05:55.060 --> 01:05:56.840
And no matter how it turns out,
无论结果如何，

1414
01:05:57.120 --> 01:06:07.400
the collective process of creating something is just wonderful and bonds you and erases fights because you can't help it but come together and make something.
共同创作的过程本身就是美妙的，它能让你建立联系，化解矛盾，因为你不得不团结一致去完成某样东西。

1415
01:06:07.580 --> 01:06:09.400
And that's what the end of that episode felt like.
那一集的结尾给人的感觉就是这样。

1416
01:06:09.400 --> 01:06:11.520
I remember everyone just standing in the bar watching the episode.
我记得大家当时都站在酒吧里看那一集。

1417
01:06:11.640 --> 01:06:13.620
And we aired the actual, you know, we played back the actual thing.
我们播出了实际的，你知道，我们回放了实际的内容。

1418
01:06:13.740 --> 01:06:14.680
It was just so lovely.
那真是太美好了。

1419
01:06:14.700 --> 01:06:16.780
And I remember seeing a cut of the episode for the first time.
我记得第一次看那一集的剪辑版。

1420
01:06:16.860 --> 01:06:19.780
And again, watching an edit of the episode was much like directing it.
再说一次，看那一集的剪辑版就像在执导它一样。

1421
01:06:19.980 --> 01:06:21.240
These guys knew what they were doing.
这些家伙知道自己在做什么。

1422
01:06:21.400 --> 01:06:23.420
You know, I don't think I had any notes.
你知道，我觉得我没什么意见。

1423
01:06:23.420 --> 01:06:27.660
I just kind of watched an office episode that I happened to have a directing credit on.
我只是看了一集《办公室》，而我恰好是这一集的导演。

1424
01:06:27.800 --> 01:06:29.200
And it has a slightly emotional ending.
它有一个略带感性的结局。

1425
01:06:29.280 --> 01:06:36.720
And I'm really proud and I'm really grateful that the writing staff was up for that at the end of the day because it makes me cherish the episode even more.
我真的很自豪，也很感激编剧团队最终愿意这样做，因为这让我更加珍惜这一集。

1426
01:06:37.340 --> 01:06:38.280
I love it too.
我也很喜欢。

1427
01:06:38.820 --> 01:06:39.720
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1428
01:06:39.860 --> 01:06:42.020
Yeah, I couldn't imagine it any other way.
是啊，我无法想象它以其他方式呈现。

1429
01:06:42.160 --> 01:06:46.540
I mean, this was such a big collective project that everyone came together for.
我的意思是，这是一个巨大的集体项目，每个人都参与其中。

1430
01:06:46.660 --> 01:06:50.700
I feel like everyone in the office would have had some kind of personal interest in it.
我觉得办公室里的每个人都会对它有某种个人兴趣。

1431
01:06:50.700 --> 01:06:53.780
And I'm so glad we were happy and reacted that way.
我很高兴我们当时很开心，并做出了那样的反应。

1432
01:06:53.940 --> 01:06:55.160
I have a confession.
我有个秘密要坦白。

1433
01:06:55.480 --> 01:06:55.800
What?
什么？

1434
01:06:56.060 --> 01:07:02.440
The very beginning of the commercial, it starts with a woman's hand taking a piece of paper off of the copier.
广告的最开始，是一个女人的手从复印机上拿走一张纸。

1435
01:07:02.700 --> 01:07:02.840
Yeah.
嗯。

1436
01:07:03.120 --> 01:07:04.860
That is supposed to be me.
那个人本该是我。

1437
01:07:05.060 --> 01:07:05.960
That's supposed to be Pam.
那本该是帕姆。

1438
01:07:06.140 --> 01:07:07.760
But I wasn't there that day.
但我那天不在场。

1439
01:07:07.760 --> 01:07:08.840
I don't know why.
我不知道为什么。

1440
01:07:08.840 --> 01:07:10.520
I was not pregnant, everybody.
大家，我当时并没有怀孕。

1441
01:07:10.520 --> 01:07:16.100
For whatever reason, they put Pam's watch and Pam's sweater on someone else.
不管什么原因，他们把帕姆的手表和毛衣穿在了别人身上。

1442
01:07:16.100 --> 01:07:17.120
I don't know.
我不知道。

1443
01:07:17.360 --> 01:07:21.000
I kind of feel like it was one of our ADs or one of our PAs.
我觉得那可能是我们的助理导演或制片助理之一。

1444
01:07:21.220 --> 01:07:23.260
So that is not my hand at the top.
所以开头那只手不是我的。

1445
01:07:23.440 --> 01:07:24.600
I did not know that.
我之前不知道这一点。

1446
01:07:24.760 --> 01:07:25.960
I am not in this either.
我也不在里面。

1447
01:07:26.440 --> 01:07:34.280
One of the things Jason said in the commentary about it that I loved is that he said filming this really reminded him of home movies he would make with his dad.
杰森在评论中提到的一点我很喜欢，他说拍摄这个过程让他想起了他小时候和父亲一起拍的家庭录像。

1448
01:07:34.440 --> 01:07:37.480
His dad is Ivan Reitman, an amazing director.
他的父亲是伊万·雷特曼，一位了不起的导演。

1449
01:07:37.480 --> 01:07:47.180
Jason said when he was a kid, he had a little handheld camera, you know, and he would make these videos like the paper airplane like that, all of that with his dad.
杰森说他小时候有一个手持摄像机，你知道，他会和父亲一起拍那些视频，比如纸飞机之类的，所有这些。

1450
01:07:47.440 --> 01:07:49.480
And it really reminded him of that.
这真的让他想起了那些时光。

1451
01:07:49.580 --> 01:07:51.060
And that's, in fact, how they shot.
事实上，他们就是这样拍摄的。

1452
01:07:51.160 --> 01:07:52.380
They shot with just a little handheld.
他们只用了一台小型手持摄像机拍摄。

1453
01:07:52.920 --> 01:08:00.700
It's funny you mentioned the paper airplane because we had a fan question from Grant Pickle who said, how did you get the shot of the paper airplane?
你提到纸飞机很有意思，因为我们收到了一位粉丝Grant Pickle的提问，他问：你们是怎么拍到纸飞机那个镜头的？

1454
01:08:01.080 --> 01:08:05.600
Well, guys, they just taped it to the front of this little handheld camera.
好吧，伙计们，他们只是把它粘在了这台小型手持摄像机的前面。

1455
01:08:05.600 --> 01:08:09.200
And Jason talked about the inspiration behind that shot.
杰森谈到了那个镜头背后的灵感来源。

1456
01:08:09.400 --> 01:08:10.680
Sam, will you play that clip?
山姆，能播放一下那个片段吗？

1457
01:08:11.180 --> 01:08:18.300
There was a shot that really became popular in the 90s and you saw it in like Sam Raimi films and John Woo filMs.
在90年代，有一种镜头非常流行，你在山姆·雷米和吴宇森的电影里都能看到。

1458
01:08:18.300 --> 01:08:27.340
I associate it with Evil Dead 2 and Army of Darkness, but also would have been popular in like literally any John Woo film where you like follow a bullet, you know,
我把它与《鬼玩人2》和《魔界英豪》联系在一起，但实际上任何吴宇森的电影里都很常见，就是那种跟随子弹的镜头，你知道的，

1459
01:08:27.420 --> 01:08:31.440
where it looks like the camera is riding on the back of a bullet or an arrow or something like that.
看起来就像摄像机骑在子弹、箭或者类似的东西上一样。

1460
01:08:31.440 --> 01:08:39.940
And I could have just imagined, you know, Michael Scott seeing any one of these films, you know, Mission Impossible 2 or like Broken Arrow or, you know, I don't know.
我完全可以想象，迈克尔·斯科特看了这些电影中的任何一部，比如《碟中谍2》或者《断箭》之类的，我不知道。

1461
01:08:40.080 --> 01:08:44.660
I don't know if Michael Scott watches the old Hong Kong films, but maybe he just saw like Van Damme and Hard Target and was like,
我不知道迈克尔·斯科特看不看老港片，但也许他只是看了尚格·云顿的《终极标靶》，然后就想，

1462
01:08:44.760 --> 01:08:47.620
we need to do a camera attached to the paper airplane shot.
我们需要拍一个把摄像机绑在纸飞机上的镜头。

1463
01:08:47.880 --> 01:08:49.860
And again, this is my favorite kind of thing.
再说一次，这是我最喜欢的那种东西。

1464
01:08:50.000 --> 01:08:52.540
It would be kind of great to make an entire movie that way.
如果能用这种方式拍整部电影应该会很棒。

1465
01:08:55.380 --> 01:08:57.740
I love how much thought went into this commercial.
我很喜欢这个广告里投入的心思。

1466
01:08:57.940 --> 01:08:58.780
It's so perfect.
它太完美了。

1467
01:08:59.080 --> 01:08:59.340
Yeah.
没错。

1468
01:08:59.660 --> 01:09:02.400
We end this episode with a little tag.
我们以一个小尾声结束这一集。

1469
01:09:02.740 --> 01:09:04.340
It's Andy's talking head.
是安迪的采访片段。

1470
01:09:04.800 --> 01:09:09.000
He's still trying to figure out the end of the Kit Kat jingle.
他还在试图搞清楚奇巧巧克力广告歌的结尾。

1471
01:09:09.360 --> 01:09:11.300
He cannot figure it out.
他怎么也想不出来。

1472
01:09:11.460 --> 01:09:13.760
And he struggles with it throughout the whole episode.
他在整集中都在为此纠结。

1473
01:09:14.020 --> 01:09:17.140
Jenna, I wrote down every single guess that Andy made.
珍娜，我记下了安迪所有的猜测。

1474
01:09:17.420 --> 01:09:21.600
Ed also mentions in the commentary that he must have improvised like 20 of these.
埃德在评论音轨里也提到，他即兴发挥了大概20个版本。

1475
01:09:21.600 --> 01:09:26.440
And he didn't know until he watched the episode, which ones made it in.
直到看了这一集，他才知道哪些被剪进去了。

1476
01:09:27.380 --> 01:09:31.800
Here's all of the wrong guesses Andy makes throughout this episode.
以下是安迪在这一集中所有错误的猜测。

1477
01:09:32.100 --> 01:09:34.000
Break me off a piece of that.
给我掰一块那个。

1478
01:09:34.520 --> 01:09:50.820
Applesauce, Chrysler Car, Football Cream, Lumber Tar, Snickers Bar, Gray Poupon, Claude Van Damme, Hair for Men, Poison Gas, NutraSweet,
苹果酱、克莱斯勒汽车、足球奶油、木材焦油、士力架、灰扑扑、克劳德·范·达美、男士生发剂、毒气、代糖，

1479
01:09:50.820 --> 01:09:54.380
and finally, Fancy FeaSt.
最后是，Fancy Feast猫粮。

1480
01:09:54.560 --> 01:09:55.780
And he's convinced.
而且他深信不疑。

1481
01:09:55.880 --> 01:09:56.660
That's it.
就是这个。

1482
01:09:56.740 --> 01:09:57.320
I did it.
我做到了。

1483
01:09:57.460 --> 01:09:58.100
Nailed it.
搞定了。

1484
01:09:58.320 --> 01:09:59.520
It's a cat food.
那是猫粮。

1485
01:09:59.780 --> 01:10:02.120
Break me off a piece of that Fancy FeaSt.
给我掰一块那个Fancy Feast猫粮。

1486
01:10:03.260 --> 01:10:04.380
So good.
太棒了。

1487
01:10:04.740 --> 01:10:08.340
Before we go, we have a final message from Jason.
在结束之前，我们有杰森发来的最后一条信息。

1488
01:10:08.940 --> 01:10:14.440
You know, my daughter, Josie, is 14, and she was a baby when I directed The Office.
你知道，我的女儿乔西14岁了，我执导《办公室》的时候她还是个婴儿。

1489
01:10:15.240 --> 01:10:19.340
And to this day, she has only seen one movie I've directed.
直到今天，她只看过我执导的一部电影。

1490
01:10:19.480 --> 01:10:22.120
In fact, up until recent, she hadn't seen any film I'd ever directed.
事实上，直到最近，她还没看过我执导的任何电影。

1491
01:10:22.200 --> 01:10:27.820
And the only thing she had ever seen that I had directed was The Office, of which she is a super fan.
她看过的我执导的唯一作品就是《办公室》，她是这部剧的超级粉丝。

1492
01:10:27.820 --> 01:10:31.420
And that made her overwhelmingly proud of me.
这让她对我感到无比自豪。

1493
01:10:31.660 --> 01:10:35.160
And it made me very grateful that I had directed The Office.
这也让我非常庆幸自己执导过《办公室》。

1494
01:10:35.440 --> 01:10:37.700
Because it put me in such high esteem of my child.
因为它让我在孩子心中拥有了很高的地位。

1495
01:10:37.920 --> 01:10:43.340
But just to say thank you, it really is a privilege to be part of the history of that show.
但还是要说声谢谢，能成为这部剧历史的一部分真的是一种荣幸。

1496
01:10:43.480 --> 01:10:45.000
Every once in a while, it'll pop up in a way.
偶尔，它总会以某种方式浮现出来。

1497
01:10:45.140 --> 01:10:47.900
Certainly when I'm doing interviews, it's one of the questions that always comes up.
当然，当我接受采访时，这总是会被问到的问题之一。

1498
01:10:47.960 --> 01:10:49.240
What was it like to direct The Office?
执导《办公室》是什么感觉？

1499
01:10:49.400 --> 01:10:52.940
Because it's kind of like, you know, there's only so many people who have walked on the moon,
因为这就像，你知道，登上过月球的人屈指可数，

1500
01:10:53.000 --> 01:10:54.680
and there's only so many people who have directed The Office.
执导过《办公室》的人也同样屈指可数。

1501
01:10:54.680 --> 01:10:56.640
And I get to be one of those people.
而我能成为其中一员。

1502
01:10:56.800 --> 01:10:58.280
I've directed two episodes, in fact.
事实上，我执导过两集。

1503
01:10:58.480 --> 01:11:01.460
And it's something that I carry really proudly.
这是我引以为傲的事情。

1504
01:11:01.680 --> 01:11:03.700
Because, you know, I didn't create that thing.
因为，你知道，那并不是我创作的。

1505
01:11:03.780 --> 01:11:04.900
I just got to be a gueSt.
我只是有幸做了一回客串。

1506
01:11:05.100 --> 01:11:09.260
You know, there's this presumption that you need to be angry to do comedy.
你知道，人们总有一种预设，认为做喜剧需要愤怒。

1507
01:11:09.680 --> 01:11:13.500
And being at The Office proves that concept wrong.
但在《办公室》剧组的经历证明这种观点是错的。

1508
01:11:14.140 --> 01:11:18.060
Because it was a group of some of the loveliest and funniest human beings I've ever met.
因为那是我见过最可爱、最风趣的一群人。

1509
01:11:18.580 --> 01:11:19.380
So sweet.
太贴心了。

1510
01:11:19.540 --> 01:11:20.280
So sweet.
太贴心了。

1511
01:11:20.540 --> 01:11:23.740
And Josie, we're so glad we helped make your dad cool.
还有乔西，我们很高兴能帮你爸爸变得很酷。

1512
01:11:24.080 --> 01:11:24.440
Yeah!
耶！

1513
01:11:24.680 --> 01:11:25.800
There you go.
就是这样。

1514
01:11:26.700 --> 01:11:29.540
Guys, thank you so much again for sending in your questions.
各位，再次非常感谢你们发来的问题。

1515
01:11:29.700 --> 01:11:31.520
And Jason, thanks for sending in all those clips.
杰森，谢谢你发来那些视频片段。

1516
01:11:31.820 --> 01:11:35.300
And we will be here next week talking about Branch Wars.
下周我们将在这里讨论《分部战争》那一集。

1517
01:11:35.960 --> 01:11:37.480
It's another hidden gem.
那是另一颗沧海遗珠。

1518
01:11:37.700 --> 01:11:40.080
I think we're going to have a few hidden gems in a row.
我觉得我们接下来会连续讨论几颗沧海遗珠。

1519
01:11:40.680 --> 01:11:41.660
I'm predicting.
我预感是这样。

1520
01:11:42.000 --> 01:11:43.180
See you next week, everybody.
下周见，大家。

1521
01:11:46.180 --> 01:11:48.160
